%% Trace: FR-10, FR-14, FR-31, FR-50–FR-52, FR-59; UC-06; SC-06; SP-06
%% Scope: Cross-service protocol using existing operation identities. No distributed transaction, activation endpoint or orphan-age deletion.
%% Legend: Each service commits only its own database. Same actor/key/payload binds one stable document identity. Handler implementation pending.
sequenceDiagram
    participant U as Authenticated author / UI
    participant W as Workspace gateway / policy
    participant WD as Workspace owned store
    participant K as Knowledge service
    participant KD as Knowledge owned store
    U->>W: Create document: title, content, explicit classification and Idempotency-Key
    W->>W: Validate session, membership, create capability and request
    alt Invalid request / denied authority / unknown authority
    W-->>U: Validation or non-disclosing denial/failure, no new content
    else Authorised request
    W->>WD: Owned transaction: bind actor/key/payload to allocated document ID, register policy, initial capabilities/read grant and audit
    alt Workspace transaction cannot durably commit
    WD-->>W: Rollback / uncertain result
    W-->>U: Explicit failure or pending outcome, reconcile same identity before retry
    else Workspace transaction confirmed or same-key replay resolved
    WD-->>W: Stable ID and original policy result, changed payload conflicts
    W->>K: Authenticated persistDocument with bound ID, actor context and operation identity
    K->>KD: Owned transaction: idempotency + immutable initial Current/passages + minimum audit
    alt Knowledge persistence confirmed
    KD-->>K: Commit / exact same-key result
    K-->>W: Confirmed document identity
    W->>W: Final protected response check under guard, expose only currently authorised response fields
    W-->>U: 201 only for confirmed result and permitted response, readiness separate
    else Timeout / lost acknowledgement / uncertain remote commit
    W-->>U: 202 pending creation, no claim of completed content or indexing
    Note over U,KD: A timeout is not cancellation. Retain registered policy, public reads reveal no content if content is absent or access denied.
    U->>W: Retry the SAME scoped key and unchanged payload
    W->>WD: Resolve original binding, do not allocate another ID or restore revoked grants
    WD-->>W: Original ID / pending identity
    W->>K: Reconcile or retry same persistence identity and immutable payload
    K-->>W: Confirmed original result or still unknown
    W-->>U: Confirmed authorised response or pending, no duplicate version/grant
    Note over U,KD: Safe default: retain inaccessible orphan policy. Cleanup needs durable cancellation/fencing proving delayed persistence cannot commit. This protocol is an explicit design gap, not an age-based sweep.
    end
    end
    end
    Note over U,KD: No Workspace activation step. Unknown remote lifecycle-write outcomes block affected protected handoffs until reconciliation. Indexing can fail independently, committed permitted keyword content does not depend on embeddings.
